Package: coreact
Title: High-Performance Co-Reactivity Analysis and Outcome Association
Version: 1.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("August F.", "Jernbom", , "ajernbom@jhmi.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7773-1851"))
Description: Optimized pipeline for calculating co-occurrence statistics
    (hypergeometric test, Jaccard index, overlap coefficient) between the
    features of two sparse binary matrices that share the same samples, or
    within one. Uses chunked sparse matrix algebra and fork-based parallel
    processing so that millions of feature pairs can be scored on a single
    node. Co-occurring pairs can then be associated with a binary or
    continuous sample-level outcome: each pair is classified by which cells
    of its 2x2 table are occupied and tested, by likelihood ratio or F test,
    on the contrast that occupancy supports (the interaction where it can),
    with profile-likelihood intervals and false discovery rate control over
    the tested contrasts. Results record their provenance, so that they can
    be re-adjusted and analysed further from disk.
